WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.200
- I like the music.

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.150
- Thank you.

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:05.160
It was so hard because I'm
always so worried about score.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.390
It always feels a little
too old and I don't know.

00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:10.020
You know how score is.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.040
It's like an overlay,
all of a sudden on your,

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.690
it's like someone else dressed
your child in crazy clothes.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:17.523
- You're right.

00:00:17.523 --> 00:00:21.080
But this is kind of
friendly, energy, and fun,

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.690
but you don't go, "Oh,
there's that tune again."

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.480
You're just like, "Yeah, that's pleasant."

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.710
(audience laughing)
- Well, if you like it,

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:32.110
then I feel good because
your ear, you're a music man.

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:37.110
And so I'm very relieved to
get your blessing on the song.

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:38.610
We've actually--

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:39.717
You know what--

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:42.716
- Drew, can I go?

00:00:42.716 --> 00:00:45.410
- Yes. (laughing)
- Come on!

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:46.270
All right, you go.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:47.520
- Oh god, I know, sorry.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.083
It's the Zoom thing.

00:00:49.083 --> 00:00:53.800
I was watching this movie and
I'm taking all these notes,

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:55.860
and all I keep thinking is

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.863
there's just not anything like this.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:01.730
- Drew, I'm telling you, the whole thing,

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:04.860
we kept saying we wanted
to do a Halloween movie.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.680
I remember when I was a kid

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:09.620
and Charlie Brown did a Halloween special,

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:12.990
and it was like, it was
the greatest thing ever

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.030
that you had something
dedicated to Halloween.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:17.255
We kind of wanted to make a movie

00:01:17.255 --> 00:01:19.777
that hopefully every year they go,

00:01:19.777 --> 00:01:21.377
"Oh yeah, let's watch "Hubie Halloween"

00:01:21.377 --> 00:01:22.610
"and get in the spirit."

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:25.160
It was shot in Salem.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.760
We all brought all our families there,

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.900
and the whole town was
decorated for Halloween.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.113
We just had a nice time together.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:35.760
- When I came to visit you up in Boston,

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:39.460
you said something to
me that stuck with me,

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:40.517
and you were like,

00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:44.507
"I still am happy when kids come up to me.

00:01:44.507 --> 00:01:47.460
"I'm still happy when
I'm talking to people."

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.740
It just made me so happy.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:54.740
The humanity of what you do,
it still burns in your heart.

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:59.770
- Drew, that's for sure.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:02.410
When you're making a movie like this,

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:05.090
I'm thinking of these kids
and I'm thinking of these,

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:06.450
I want families to have a good time.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.170
I want every age to laugh,

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:11.720
but when a little kid comes up to you,

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.930
and calls you by the
character's name from the movie

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:18.450
and kids come up to me while I'm eating,

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:19.930
I'll stop eating and hang out with--

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.680
By the way, it's very hard
for me to stop eating,

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:22.550
you know that.

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:25.070
But I will stop eating
and talk to the kids

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:27.010
as long as they want to talk.

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:29.100
- By the way, I just got so excited.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.540
There was like a hot debate on Twitter

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:34.300
about you, me, and Aniston.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.040
- Yes. I heard about this, Drew,

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.743
and you told me that it was fun.

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:43.430
That's Jennifer Aniston right there.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:44.900
You see how you did it with a picture?

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:45.950
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:47.420
We have that technology.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.460
Of course the picture I'm
referring to you, me, and J

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:52.370
is literally a Polaroid.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:53.760
- I know, we had fun with J, by the way.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.330
But yes, and Drew, I remember
you crossing your eyes

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:57.163
for that picture.

00:02:57.163 --> 00:02:59.616
And remember, that stuck
for about four days.

00:02:59.616 --> 00:03:01.866
(laughing)

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:05.300
Yeah. I love that.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:08.260
I love you. And you know I
love Aniston and so do you.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:10.126
We're all great friends.

00:03:10.126 --> 00:03:14.310
And some debate that sounded nuts to me.

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:18.680
- I loved it because what I
wanted to do is respond to say,

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:20.180
I would pick her too.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:22.120
And let everyone know

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:25.620
that we all are kind of like a triangle

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:29.020
and there's not only no
competition, but so much love.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:31.140
And then I thought about doing something

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:33.250
with you, me, and her, where I choose her

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:35.490
and run off into the sunset.

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:38.657
- Anybody who sees the three
of us together would be like,

00:03:38.657 --> 00:03:40.137
"Sandman, you got to go, man.

00:03:40.137 --> 00:03:41.407
"You don't belong with those two.

00:03:41.407 --> 00:03:44.707
"Those are two nice,
smart, good looking ladies.

00:03:44.707 --> 00:03:46.720
"You're pathetic. Beat it."

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:49.300
But somehow I lucked in
to both of your lives.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.510
So I'm staying there.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:53.160
- Maybe just the three of
us should do something.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:54.120
- I would do that.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.512
You just tell me your new schedule, Drew.

00:03:56.512 --> 00:03:59.583
When you can do movies now
with the Drew show going on.

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:06.670
- I've really never wanted
to do anything important

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:08.360
in this world and in my life

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:11.820
that isn't a side-by-side with you.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:13.500
So thank you.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.980
And look out for my love Adam

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:20.090
on what I am sure to be an annual must

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:24.690
in "Hubie Halloween"
streaming on Netflix now.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:26.020
I love you.

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:26.853
- I love you.

00:04:26.853 --> 00:04:28.480
Drew, thank you, thank you, thank you.

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.236
I love you, baby.
- Forever

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:32.819
(upbeat music)

